    Fix diagram and proof for two-index search

    $lo itself is excluded through $mid+1 as usual,
    and $hi is excluded by... just being $mid itself.
    Should $array->[$hi-1] be the last equal value
    the upper bound would collapse to $hi; but the
    lower bound is still just set to $lo as there is
    a chance that one index above the just-excluded
    value is the first match we want; i.e. $mid+1,
    which is just $lo.

    the diagram should exclude the just-found index
    too (with the "o" being a trace of the $mid's...)

